<template>
    <SiteShell page="features">
        <div class="page-head">
            <h1>Features</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                One drawing model behind inspection, exchange and agent
                authoring. Create, edit, undo/redo, manage layers, import a
                declared DXF subset, save, inspect and export a drawing today;
                the interactive viewport and STEP/STL output are labelled as
                unfinished instead of being implied by a suffix.
            </p>
            <div class="head-tags">
                <span class="chip chip--available">document core available</span>
                <span class="chip chip--blocked">viewport not implemented</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Contracts</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid-2">
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Handle API</h3>
                    <p>
                        Create, open, save, undo/redo, layer and entity editing,
                        DXF import, inspect, export and close all take a handle.
                        The SDK returns a document wrapper, so one drawing is
                        mutated instead of a path being re-guessed at each step.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Revisions</h3>
                    <p>
                        Every mutation increments the revision, and saved files
                        reopen at the revision they were written with. Inspection
                        findings carry the revision they were computed from.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Stable error codes</h3>
                    <p>
                        Failures carry a code such as <code>format/invalid</code>
                        or <code>capability/not-implemented</code>. The studio
                        parses the code, keeps the message and never turns a
                        rejection into a success state.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--declared">measured</span>
                    <h3>Per-format matrix</h3>
                    <p>
                        DWG, DXF, STEP, STP, IGES, IGS, STL, OBJ, SVG, PDF, PNG
                        and JPG are registered. SVG, DXF and PDF are supported
                        export targets; DXF also has a declared ASCII import
                        subset. Nothing else imports.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Feature areas</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--blocked">read the status</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid-3">
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Drawing document</h3>
                    <p>
                        `.ocad` projects hold ordered layers, a revision, a unit
                        and a flat entity list. Save writes a temporary file and
                        renames it into place; open validates tag, version,
                        identity and coordinates.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Entity editing</h3>
                    <p>
                        Lines, circles, polylines, text and linear dimensions can
                        be added, listed, moved, updated and deleted through the
                        SDK, the CLI and the native JSON-RPC surface. Geometry on
                        a locked layer refuses with <code>drawing/layer-locked</code>.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Undo and layers</h3>
                    <p>
                        Each handle keeps 32 bounded snapshots. Undo and redo
                        restore a snapshot, bump the revision and report
                        <code>canUndo</code>/<code>canRedo</code>. Layers can be
                        added, renamed with atomic reference updates, hidden and
                        locked.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Inspection</h3>
                    <p>
                        Units, layers, geometry and dimensions run today and
                        report per-object findings, including hidden or locked
                        layers, duplicate layer names, empty text and zero-length
                        segments. Constraints and references refuse.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">partial</span>
                    <h3>Exchange</h3>
                    <p>
                        SVG keeps layer colours and every entity. DXF is ASCII R12
                        with a HEADER, LAYER table and LINE/CIRCLE/TEXT entities,
                        plus a loss report. PDF is a minimal vector A4 landscape
                        page. DXF import reads only the declared subset.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">shell only</span>
                    <h3>Studio</h3>
                    <p>
                        Titlebar, path field, layer rail with visibility and lock
                        controls, undo/redo, DXF import, inspector tabs and status
                        bar work against the native host. The viewport is still a
                        frame and says so.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">executable</span>
                    <h3>Agent skills</h3>
                    <p>
                        The skill document lists the real commands and the real
                        limits. It never presents the viewport or STEP/STL output
                        as available, and it states the DXF import subset.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

