                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">CLI</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--available">available</span></td>
                            <td>Creates, edits, undoes/redoes, manages layers, imports DXF, inspects and exports drawings. Editing commands save the file in place.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">SDK</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--available">available</span></td>
                            <td>Returns a handle-backed document with undo/redo, layers, entity editing, import, inspect, save, export, delete and list.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">Studio</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--declared">shell only</span></td>
                            <td>Sends the documented JSON-RPC requests, offers undo/redo, import and layer controls, and never paints geometry.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">Skills</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--available">executable</span></td>
                            <td>Records the routing rules and the exact commands that work in this build.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Format honesty</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--declared">measured</span>
            </div>
            <p>
                The format registry classifies DWG, DXF, STEP, STP, IGES, IGS, STL,
                OBJ, SVG, PDF, PNG and JPG, but classification is not a support
                claim. <code>capabilities()</code> reports SVG, DXF, PDF, STL and
                STEP as supported export targets, DXF and STEP as partial
                formats, the native project as partial, and the PNG renderer as
                unsupported. STEP output is a faceted BREP projection of closed
                profiles, not a modelling kernel.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
